=head1 DESCRIPTION

The automated response to a risk level for adaptive authentication in
full-function, or C<ENFORCED>, mode. You can assign an action to each
risk level that threat protection evaluates.

=head1 ATTRIBUTES


=head2 B<REQUIRED> EventAction => Str

The action to take for the attempted account takeover action for the
associated risk level. Valid values are as follows:

=over

=item *

C<BLOCK>: Block the request.

=item *

C<MFA_IF_CONFIGURED>: Present an MFA challenge if possible. MFA is
possible if the user pool has active MFA methods that the user can set
up. For example, if the user pool only supports SMS message MFA but the
user doesn't have a phone number attribute, MFA setup isn't possible.
If MFA setup isn't possible, allow the request.

=item *

C<MFA_REQUIRED>: Present an MFA challenge if possible. Block the
request if a user hasn't set up MFA. To sign in with required MFA,
users must have an email address or phone number attribute, or a
registered TOTP factor.

=item *

C<NO_ACTION>: Take no action. Permit sign-in.

=back



=head2 B<REQUIRED> Notify => Bool

Determines whether Amazon Cognito sends a user a notification message
when your user pools assesses a user's session at the associated risk
level.



